course: dictionary
lesson: 7174
title: Strong words and their clues
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Persecute is a strong word. To persecute people is to treat them cruelly and unfairly for a long time, often because of their religion, race, beliefs or who they are. Look at the context: «Early Christians were persecuted by Roman rulers.» The words cruelly and unfairly are clues that the word is about something bad being done to people.
explain: Clues often come from the words around the word. «Many groups, such as Jews, have been persecuted through history.» The word through history tells you this has happened again and again over a long time. Persecution is about injustice, which means people are treated badly when they have done nothing wrong.
explain: Persecute can also mean to keep annoying or bothering someone. This is a smaller meaning, and it is not the one used in history lessons. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If the sentence is about a whole group being treated cruelly for who they are, the strong meaning is the right one.
fact: Persecute means to treat people cruelly and unfairly for a long time, often because of their religion, race, beliefs or who they are.
fact: Persecuted is the past tense of persecute, and persecuting is the -ing form.
fact: «Flee persecution» means to run away to escape cruel and unfair treatment.
fact: Persecute can also mean to keep annoying or bothering someone, but this meaning is less common in history.
fact: Persecution is wrong, and ethics lessons teach that people should be treated fairly whatever they believe.
exercise: «Many groups have been persecuted through history.» What does persecuted mean here? | *Treated cruelly and unfairly for a long time | Asked to move house | Given many fine presents | Made to laugh loudly
exercise: «Some early Christians fled persecution.» What does flee persecution mean? | *Run away to escape cruel and unfair treatment | Write a famous book | Stay and build a bigger house | Ask for a free holiday
exercise: Jesus said, «Love your enemies and pray for those who persecute you.» What does persecute mean in this sentence? | Sing a song with you | *Treat you cruelly and unfairly | Give you a gift
test: Persecuted people are usually treated | *Unfairly and cruelly | Only once, for one day | Kindly and fairly | Like guests at a party
test: «Christians were sometimes persecuted, but the faith kept growing.» Which word is a clue that persecuted is a bad thing? | Christians | growing | faith | *but
exam: Persecute can mean to keep annoying or bothering someone. Which word is the closest synonym? | Protect | Feed | Praise | *Pester
